    "slug": "ai-governance-vs-compliance",
    "title": "AI Governance vs AI Compliance: What's the Difference?",
    "description": "AI governance and AI compliance are related, but they are not the same thing. Confusing them leads to buying the wrong tools and missing the wrong risks.",
    "ogTitle": "AI Governance vs AI Compliance: What's the Difference?",
    "ogDescription": "AI governance and AI compliance are related, but they are not the same thing. Confusing them leads to buying the wrong tools and missing the wrong risks.",
    "ogImage": "https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png",
    "canonical": "https://csoai.org/blog/ai-governance-vs-compliance",
    "css": ".legacy-content { color: #E8E4F0; line-height: 1.7; }\n.legacy-content h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; }\n.legacy-content h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }\n.legacy-content h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #E8B76D; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }\n.legacy-content p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n.legacy-content ul, .legacy-content ol { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.5rem; padding-left: 1rem; }\n.legacy-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }\n.legacy-content a { color: #10b981; text-decoration: underline; }\n.legacy-content strong { color: #D4A843; font-weight: 700; }\n.legacy-content em { font-style: italic; color: rgba(232, 228, 240, 0.85); }",
    "content": "<main>\n<h2>The words are not interchangeable</h2>\n<p>AI governance and AI compliance are related, but they are not the same thing. Confusing them leads to buying the wrong tools and missing the wrong risks.</p>\n<h2>AI governance</h2>\n<p>Governance is the ongoing system of oversight. It includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Roles and responsibilities</li>\n<li>Decision rights and escalation paths</li>\n<li>Policies and principles</li>\n<li>Risk appetite</li>\n<li>Board and executive accountability</li>\n<li>Stakeholder engagement</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Governance asks: <em>Who decides what is acceptable, and how do they decide it?</em></p>\n<h2>AI compliance</h2>\n<p>Compliance is the demonstration that specific obligations are met. It includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mapping systems to regulatory requirements</li>\n<li>Documenting controls and evidence</li>\n<li>Producing attestations and audit trails</li>\n<li>Responding to regulator requests</li>\n<li>Meeting deadlines like the EU AI Act Article 50 transparency obligation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compliance asks: <em>Can we prove we meet the rules that apply to us?</em></p>\n<h2>Why the distinction matters</h2>\n<p>You can have good governance and still fail compliance if you cannot produce evidence. You can pass a compliance check and still have bad governance if decisions are opaque or unaccountable.</p>\n<p>Most organisations need both. But the tools are different.</p>\n<h2>Governance without compliance is a talking shop</h2>\n<p>A well-written AI ethics policy is governance. It is necessary but not sufficient. When a regulator asks for technical documentation, risk management records, and human oversight evidence, the policy alone will not satisfy them.</p>\n<h2>Compliance without governance is a checkbox exercise</h2>\n<p>A vendor that generates documentation without involving your risk owners, board, or operational teams creates compliance theatre. It might pass an audit today, but it will not survive a serious incident or a change in leadership.</p>\n<h2>How CSOAI addresses both</h2>\n<p>Layer 0 is built for governance <em>and</em> compliance:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>designed 33-agent council</strong> — distributed decision rights for high-stakes attestation and revocation decisions.</li>\n<li><strong>did:csoai identity</strong> — clear accountability for every agent.</li>\n<li><strong>Ed25519-signed attestations</strong> — verifiable evidence of compliance state.</li>\n<li><strong>Hash-chained audit trail</strong> — proof of what was decided, when, and by whom.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Governance sets the rules. Compliance proves they are followed. Layer 0 records both.</p>\n<p><strong>Learn more:</strong> https://csoai.org/layer0</p>\n</main>",
