    "ogTitle": "DORA Compliance for UK Financial Services",
    "ogDescription": "The Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) applies to financial entities operating in the EU from 17 January 2025. It requires firms to ensure they can wi...",
    "ogImage": "https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png",
    "canonical": "https://csoai.org/blog/dora-compliance-uk-financial-services",
    "css": ".legacy-content { color: #E8E4F0; line-height: 1.7; }\n.legacy-content h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; }\n.legacy-content h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }\n.legacy-content h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #E8B76D; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }\n.legacy-content p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n.legacy-content ul, .legacy-content ol { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.5rem; padding-left: 1rem; }\n.legacy-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }\n.legacy-content a { color: #10b981; text-decoration: underline; }\n.legacy-content strong { color: #D4A843; font-weight: 700; }\n.legacy-content em { font-style: italic; color: rgba(232, 228, 240, 0.85); }",
    "content": "<main>\n<h2>What is DORA?</h2>\n<p>The Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) applies to financial entities operating in the EU from 17 January 2025. It requires firms to ensure they can withstand, respond to, and recover from all types of ICT-related disruptions and threats.</p>\n<p>UK firms serving EU customers are in scope. UK regulators are also aligning domestic rules with DORA principles.</p>\n<h2>The five pillars</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>ICT risk management</strong> — governance, identification, and mitigation</li>\n<li><strong>ICT-related incident management</strong> — detection, reporting, and recovery</li>\n<li><strong>Digital operational resilience testing</strong> — threat-led penetration testing</li>\n<li><strong>Managing third-party risk</strong> — due diligence on ICT service providers</li>\n<li><strong>Information sharing</strong> — appropriate sharing of cyber threat intelligence</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Where AI systems fit in</h2>\n<p>AI is increasingly part of the ICT infrastructure that financial firms rely on. If your firm uses AI for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Credit decisions</li>\n<li>Fraud detection</li>\n<li>Trading algorithms</li>\n<li>Customer onboarding</li>\n<li>Anti-money laundering checks</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then DORA applies to those systems. You must be able to demonstrate resilience, incident response capability, and third-party oversight.</p>\n<h2>Attestation as evidence</h2>\n<p>DORA requires evidence, not promises. A signed attestation that maps your AI system&#x27;s controls to DORA requirements gives regulators and auditors a concrete artefact to review.</p>\n<p>CSOAI&#x27;s DORA-aligned MCP servers and attestation API can generate:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>ICT risk classification</li>\n<li>Incident response readiness evidence</li>\n<li>Third-party dependency mapping</li>\n<li>Resilience testing records</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All signed with Ed25519 and publicly verifiable.</p>\n<h2>What to do now</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Map your AI systems to DORA&#x27;s five pillars.</li>\n<li>Identify third-party AI/ICT providers and assess their resilience.</li>\n<li>Document incident response procedures.</li>\n<li>Generate attestations for high-risk systems.</li>\n<li>Test your resilience under realistic failure scenarios.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>DORA is not a one-off checkbox. It is a continuous resilience programme.</p>\n<p><strong>Start with an attestation:</strong> https://csoai.org/dora</p>\n</main>",
    "ldJson": ["{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n  \"headline\": \"DORA Compliance for UK Financial Services\",\n  \"description\": \"The Digital Operational Resilience Act (DORA) applies to financial entities operating in the EU from 17 January 2025. It requires firms to ensure they can wi...\",\n  \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/blog/dora-compliance-uk-financial-services\",\n  \"datePublished\": \"2026-06-17\",\n  \"author\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\"\n  },\n  \"publisher\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\",\n    \"logo\": {\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png\"\n    }\n  }\n}"]
