    "description": "If you are a UK company building AI systems, there is a high chance you qualify for R&D tax credits. Many founders overlook this because \"R&D\" sounds like la...",
    "ogTitle": "R&D Tax Credits: The Most Overlooked Cash Source for UK AI Startups",
    "ogDescription": "If you are a UK company building AI systems, there is a high chance you qualify for R&D tax credits. Many founders overlook this because \"R&D\" sounds like la...",
    "ogImage": "https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png",
    "canonical": "https://csoai.org/blog/rd-tax-credits-uk-ai-startups",
    "css": ".legacy-content { color: #E8E4F0; line-height: 1.7; }\n.legacy-content h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; }\n.legacy-content h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }\n.legacy-content h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #E8B76D; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }\n.legacy-content p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n.legacy-content ul, .legacy-content ol { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.5rem; padding-left: 1rem; }\n.legacy-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }\n.legacy-content a { color: #10b981; text-decoration: underline; }\n.legacy-content strong { color: #D4A843; font-weight: 700; }\n.legacy-content em { font-style: italic; color: rgba(232, 228, 240, 0.85); }",
    "content": "<main>\n<h2>Free money you are probably already entitled to</h2>\n<p>If you are a UK company building AI systems, there is a high chance you qualify for R&amp;D tax credits. Many founders overlook this because &quot;R&amp;D&quot; sounds like lab coats and particle accelerators. It is not.</p>\n<p>For tax purposes, R&amp;D is any project that seeks to achieve an advance in science or technology through the resolution of scientific or technological uncertainty.</p>\n<p>Building a new AI governance framework? R&amp;D. Designing a novel cryptographic attestation chain? R&amp;D. Creating a designed 33-agent council for high-stakes compliance decisions? R&amp;D.</p>\n<h2>What can you claim?</h2>\n<p>For SMEs, the R&amp;D tax credit scheme allows you to deduct an extra 86% of qualifying R&amp;D spend from your taxable profits (from April 2023). If you are loss-making, you can surrender the loss for a cash credit worth up to 14.5% of the surrenderable loss.</p>\n<p>In practical terms, for every £100 of qualifying R&amp;D spend, a loss-making SME can receive up to £18.60 in cash.</p>\n<h2>What counts as qualifying spend?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Staff costs (salaries, NI, pension contributions) for people working directly on R&amp;D</li>\n<li>Externally provided workers and subcontractors (with restrictions)</li>\n<li>Software and cloud costs used directly in R&amp;D</li>\n<li>Consumable materials</li>\n<li>Clinical trial volunteers</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Common qualifying activities for AI companies</h2>\n<p>If your team does any of the following, you likely have a claim:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Training custom machine-learning models</li>\n<li>Designing new architectures for inference, consensus, or verification</li>\n<li>Building bespoke evaluation or audit tooling</li>\n<li>Resolving uncertainty around model behaviour, fairness, or robustness</li>\n<li>Integrating emerging protocols (A2A, MCP, ACP, x402) in novel ways</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What does not count</h2>\n<p>Routine development, bug fixes, market research, and commercialisation activities generally do not qualify. The key test is uncertainty: did you genuinely not know whether the approach would work when you started?</p>\n<h2>The documentation you need</h2>\n<p>You do not need a formal lab notebook, but you do need evidence:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technical specifications and architecture documents</li>\n<li>Git commit history showing iteration and experimentation</li>\n<li>Notes on failed approaches and why they failed</li>\n<li>Time records for R&amp;D staff</li>\n<li>Contractor invoices and cloud receipts</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Our claim</h2>\n<p>At CSOAI, we are preparing an R&amp;D tax credit claim for 2025–2026 covering work on Layer 0, the Council engine, and the 6-layer cryptographic disclosure stack. Estimated qualifying spend: £74,000. Estimated return: ~£24,420.</p>\n<p>If you are a UK AI founder and you are not claiming R&amp;D tax credits, you are leaving money on the table.</p>\n<p><strong>Need help?</strong> Speak to a UK R&amp;D tax specialist or your accountant. The deadline is within two years of your accounting period end.</p>\n</main>",
    "ldJson": ["{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n  \"headline\": \"R&D Tax Credits: The Most Overlooked Cash Source for UK AI Startups\",\n  \"description\": \"If you are a UK company building AI systems, there is a high chance you qualify for R&D tax credits. Many founders overlook this because \\\"R&D\\\" sounds like la...\",\n  \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/blog/rd-tax-credits-uk-ai-startups\",\n  \"datePublished\": \"2026-06-17\",\n  \"author\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\"\n  },\n  \"publisher\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\",\n    \"logo\": {\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png\"\n    }\n  }\n}"]
