    "slug": "sovereign-governance-layer",
    "title": "Announcing the Council Governance Layer: Per-Cell Evidence for EU AI Act Compliance | CSOAI Blog",
    "description": "CSOAI opens the Council Governance Layer: Bench-as-a-Service per evaluation and a Governance Fine-tune Recipe per engagement, under an honesty contract \u2014 per-cell evidence only, no composites, UNMEASURED labelled.",
    "ogTitle": "Announcing the Council Governance Layer: Per-Cell Evidence for EU AI Act Compliance",
    "ogDescription": "CSOAI opens the Council Governance Layer: Bench-as-a-Service per evaluation and a Governance Fine-tune Recipe per engagement, under an honesty contract \u2014 per-cell evidence only, no composites, UNMEASURED labelled.",
    "ogImage": "https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png",
    "canonical": "https://csoai.org/blog/sovereign-governance-layer",
    "css": ".legacy-content { color: #E8E4F0; line-height: 1.7; }\n.legacy-content h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.2; }\n.legacy-content h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); font-weight: 700; color: #FFFFFF; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }\n.legacy-content h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #E8B76D; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }\n.legacy-content p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }\n.legacy-content ul, .legacy-content ol { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.5rem; padding-left: 1rem; }\n.legacy-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }\n.legacy-content a { color: #10b981; text-decoration: underline; }\n.legacy-content strong { color: #D4A843; font-weight: 700; }\n.legacy-content em { font-style: italic; color: rgba(232, 228, 240, 0.85); }",
    "content": "<main>\n<h2>What are we announcing?</h2>\n<p>Today CSOAI Ltd (UK Companies House 16939677, registered office 3rd Floor, 86-90 Paul Street, London EC2A 4NE) opens the <a href=\"/governance-layer\">Council Governance Layer</a> to commercial engagements. It is an instrument, not a badge: a measurement service that produces per-cell evidence about what your AI systems actually do under a frozen benchmark, and labels whatever it cannot measure as UNMEASURED rather than papering over the gap.</p>\n<p>The timing is deliberate. On <strong>2 August 2026</strong>, the EU AI Act&#x27;s <strong>Article 50</strong> transparency duties begin to apply, and every AI company placing systems on the European market will need evidence \u2014 not intentions \u2014 about disclosure, synthetic-content marking, and governance controls. The Council Governance Layer exists to produce exactly that evidence, in a form you can hand to a customer, an auditor, or a regulator.</p>\n\n<h2>What do you actually buy?</h2>\n<p>Two offers, priced GBP-first with a USD toggle:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bench-as-a-Service (per evaluation).</strong> We run your system against a frozen benchmark \u2014 currently 417 frozen provisions drawn from 9+ frameworks, organised along the four GSPC axes: Governance, Safety, Provenance, and Continuity. You receive the full per-cell results matrix: every provision, every asset, every measurement, with method and raw output attached. No composite score. No star rating. No roll-up that hides the failures.</li>\n<li><strong>Governance Fine-tune Recipe (per engagement).</strong> A scoped engagement that takes the failures the bench surfaces and converts them into a concrete remediation recipe: which controls to add, which disclosures to wire in, which MCP servers in your estate to bring under governance instrumentation, and how to re-measure afterwards so the improvement is demonstrated rather than asserted.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What is the honesty contract?</h2>\n<p>Every engagement runs under three rules, and they are written into the deliverable itself:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Per-cell evidence only.</strong> Each measured cell stands alone with its own data and its own method note. If a cell failed, you see the failure.</li>\n<li><strong>No composites.</strong> We do not average cells into a reassuring single number, because composites are where bad cells go to hide. If a provision was not run against an asset, that cell is labelled <strong>UNMEASURED</strong> \u2014 visibly, permanently, and counted as unmeasured in every summary.</li>\n<li><strong>Retractions are public.</strong> When our own prior claims fail re-measurement, the correction goes on the <a href=\"/refutation-ledger\">refutation ledger</a>, including own-bet retractions such as the n_eff = 1.21 quorum refutation. Our wager is that you trust an instrument more when you can watch it correct itself.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Why does this matter for EU AI Act evidence?</h2>\n<p>Because Article 50 is a transparency obligation with fines attached. Providers of AI systems that interact with people must disclose, at the point of interaction, that the user is dealing with a machine. Providers of systems that generate synthetic content must mark it as machine-generated in a machine-readable way. Systems that infer emotions or perform biometric categorisation must inform the people exposed. Non-compliance with these duties sits in the Article 99 penalty tier of up to <strong>&#x20AC;15 million or 3% of global annual turnover</strong>; prohibited practices carry ceilings of <strong>&#x20AC;35 million or 7%</strong>. Our <a href=\"/article-50\">Article 50 guide</a> walks through the obligations in plain English.</p>\n<p>An attestation-grade measurement record \u2014 what your system discloses, what it marks, and precisely where the gaps are \u2014 is the raw material of a defensible position. That is what the bench produces.</p>\n\n<h2>What does the instrumentation actually cover?</h2>\n<p>The governance estate behind the offer is public and inspectable: <strong>570 public repositories</strong> on GitHub under CSOAI-ORG, with <strong>291 governed MCP servers</strong> wired into the measurement harness. The bench freezes <strong>417 provisions across 9+ frameworks</strong> so results are comparable run-over-run and cannot be quietly re-normed after the fact. The <a href=\"/govbench\">GovBench</a> surface shows the provision structure; the <a href=\"/leaderboard\">leaderboard</a> shows measured cells \u2014 including the empty ones.</p>\n\n<h2>What do we refuse to claim?</h2>\n<p>Our own benchmark run is the reference example of the discipline we sell. The ProvBench finding reads, verbatim: <em>&#x201C;0 of 20 assets survived (0 of 180 measured cells). One-sided 95% Clopper&#x2013;Pearson 13.9% (two-sided 16.8%). Interval computed at n=20 assets, not n=180 cells.&#x201D;</em> That result includes our own systems. We publish it because an instrument that only reports good news is not an instrument. The full methodology is at <a href=\"/provenance-finding\">/provenance-finding</a>.</p>\n<p>We measure. We attest to what was measured. We label the rest UNMEASURED. That is the whole product.</p>\n<p><strong>Book an evaluation at <a href=\"/governance-layer\">/governance-layer</a>. Audit our failures first at <a href=\"/refutation-ledger\">/refutation-ledger</a>.</strong></p>\n</main>",
    "ldJson": ["{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\n  \"headline\": \"Announcing the Council assistant Governance Layer: Per-Cell Evidence for EU AI Act Compliance\",\n  \"description\": \"CSOAI opens the Council assistant Governance Layer: Bench-as-a-Service per evaluation and a Governance Fine-tune Recipe per engagement, under an honesty contract \\u2014 per-cell evidence only, no composites, UNMEASURED labelled.\",\n  \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/blog/sovereign-governance-layer\",\n  \"datePublished\": \"2026-08-01\",\n  \"author\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\"\n  },\n  \"publisher\": {\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n    \"name\": \"CSOAI\",\n    \"logo\": {\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csoai.org/assets/og-image.png\"\n    }\n  }\n}"]
